From b8a699bd12ade303492666fcb3886697f706b771 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luomeng Zhou <luomeng@merqube.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 16:42:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Add put harvesting for option strategies indices

Adds an early-rebalance condition and treatment that close an appreciated
protective put and re-strike it lower, for collar strategies that monetise
protection instead of letting it decay.

PutHarvestEarlyRebalance fires when a long put is in the money, has reached a
multiple of its entry premium, and still has time left. It is assessed only on
the roll schedule's own dates rather than every calculation date.

The entry premium is recovered by re-pricing the contract on the date it was
opened, so nothing has to be persisted for positions opened by the normal roll.
Positions opened off-schedule by a harvest do need it, hence the new optional
RollingOptionPosition.entry_date -- without it a re-struck put is measured
against the original contract's premium and re-triggers immediately.

RestrikeAtMarketEarlyRebalTreatment books the market premium rather than
intrinsic value: the existing treatments settle at max(spot - strike, 0), which
is right for an exercise but discards the time value a harvest exists to
capture. The replacement keeps the same expiry, so the tranche stays on its roll
cycle, and its cost is netted against the proceeds with only the remainder
reinvested.

Two engine fixes were needed to make an early rebalance that opens a position
work at all:

* Close prices are loaded before the pre-level step runs, so a position the step
  opens is unpriced. MOIPreCalcStep now fetches prices for anything it finds
  unpriced afterwards.
* compute_eod then passed its own local reference to those prices on to
  create_post_close. Pydantic copies the dict when IndexDailyPrices is built, so
  prices added during the step never reached the post-close workflow and the
  level computation failed on them. It now re-reads from the model.

Also narrows the backwards-compatibility shim on EarlyRebalanceSpec. It used to
tag any untyped condition as the legacy one; a harvest config missing its
discriminator was therefore parsed as OptionStrategiesEarlyRebalance with every
harvest parameter silently dropped, and the index ran early-exercise testing
instead. Only a condition whose fields the legacy model understands is tagged
now.

FT_Aug_12 is the SPY collar this was built for: ATM puts laddered in four
quarterly tranches of one-year trades, against short bi-weekly 2% OTM calls.

NEEDS A DECISION BEFORE MERGE: the annual-tranching guard in strategies/spec.py
is commented out here, carried over as-is from local backtesting, because the
put leg is exactly what it rejects (number_of_tranches=4 with a 12-month roll).
The guard was added for PE-8350 after a production failure and is correct for
most configurations -- a 4-tranche annual ladder anchored to January lands on
Apr/Jul/Oct, which have no twelve-month expiries. It is wrong only for a ladder
anchored to the quarterly cycle, which is what FT_Aug_12 uses. Narrowing it to
check tranche start months needs no data access and would let both cases be
enforced; that is the change to agree on rather than shipping it commented out.

